  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YEM027N Strengthening Community Capacity in Peacebuilding (2)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To achieve the goal of Yemeni women having greater influence in fostering durable peace and inclusive public decision-making at local and sub-national levels, CARE is proposing a three-pronged approach: 
1.	Provide capacity-building for Yemeni CSOs and Yemeni women&#x2019;s groups working on grassroots peacebuilding; and 
2.	Promote gender equality amongst Yemeni youth groups and support them to engage in advocacy and their communities; and 
3.	Promote gender equality amongst influential men. 

Overarching ToC: 
IF CSOs and women&#x2019;s groups have enhanced knowledge and capacities and have gained opportunities in decision-making and peacebuilding; which are supported with resources, actionable learning and spaces to collaboratively address drivers of local conflict and inequality;
AND Youth groups have enhanced capacities and knowledge in gender equality, decision-making, and peacebuilding and linkages with CSO&#x2019;s and women&#x2019;s groups; with the understanding they are the future leaders and decision-makers;
AND Decision-makers have embraced and contributed to an enabling environment for peacebuilding and inclusive gender norms, thereby supporting youth and women&#x2019;s participation in decision-making; 
THEN Women and youth will influence local peacebuilding initiatives and participate in inclusive decision-making, a proven contributor to durable peace.</narrative>
  </description>
